{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>He has not beheld iniquity in Jacob, etc.</b> As the Targum renders. Another interpretation, after its plain sense — it is expounded as a fine midrash:" "<b>He has not beheld.</b> The Holy One, blessed be He — the <b>iniquity</b> that is in Jacob: when they transgress His word, He does not scrutinize them to examine their iniquities and the trouble they take to transgress His law:" "<b>Trouble.</b> A term for transgression, as in ״וְהָרָה עָמָל״ (Psalms 7), ״כִּי אַתָּה עָמָל וָכַעַס תַּבִּיט״ (ibid. 10) — because transgression is trouble before the Omnipresent." "<b>YHWH his Elohim is with him.</b> Even when they provoke and rebel before Him, He does not move from among them." "<b>And the King's friendship is in him.</b> A term of affection and friendship, as in (II Samuel 15) ״רֵעֶה דָּוִד״ — a lover of David, (Judges 15) ״וַיִּתְּנָהּ לְמֵרֵעֵהוּ״, and so Onkelos renders: ״וּשְׁכִינַת מַלְכְהוֹן בֵּינֵהוֹן״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:28.928969269Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}